Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/TerminalDxe: serial control keys match Ctrl registrations

Since 184fb6b1035e ("MdeModulePkg/TerminalDxe: Fix handling of shift
state in notifications", issue #12281, first in edk2-stable202608),
IsKeyRegistered requires a registration's KeyShiftState to equal the
input key's, ignoring only EFI_SHIFT_STATE_VALID. A terminal carries no
shift state: TerminalDxe gives every key it reads shift state 0
(EfiKeyFiFoInsertOneKey, KeyNotifyProcessHandler). Upstream accepted
that notifications with a shift state then never fire on a terminal.
But the UEFI Shell registers its break as 0x03 (and 'c') with
EFI_LEFT_CONTROL_PRESSED or EFI_RIGHT_CONTROL_PRESSED, and its pause as
0x13 (and 's') the same way, so a serial Ctrl-C (0x03) matches none of
them: it no longer stops a running command, and the prompt comes back
only when the command ends.

When the input key carries no shift state (0, or EFI_SHIFT_STATE_VALID
alone) and is a control character 0x01-0x1A (Ctrl+A to Ctrl+Z as a
terminal sends them) other than Backspace, Tab, LF and CR (0x08, 0x09,
0x0A, 0x0D), a registration whose shift state is only Control (left,
right or both, with or without EFI_SHIFT_STATE_VALID) matches. Those
four are left out because a terminal sends them for keys of their own,
not for Ctrl chords: with them, plain typing with Enter fired a Ctrl+M
registration, such as a stale one left on a keyboard device that has
gone, whose function then runs from freed memory. Every other case
keeps #12281's exact comparison, so RCtrl+n still does not fire on a
plain 'n', and the toggle state is still compared exactly. The fix is
here, not in ShellPkg, so that it serves every registrant of a Ctrl key
(any Shell binary, any application), as edk2-stable202605 and earlier
did. Those ignored the shift state for every key, BS, TAB, LF and CR
included; this patch does not restore that for those four.

RegisterKeyNotify's duplicate check calls IsKeyRegistered too: there a
new registration of a control character with no shift state, for a
function already registered for that character with Control held, gets
the existing handle, as before 184fb6b1035e: both registrations then
share one entry, and unregistering it removes it for both. BS, TAB, LF
and CR are compared exactly there too.

axl-firmware's patch against edk2-stable202611, applied after
0003-map-debug-uart.patch to a copy of the packages it touches.

---
diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Console/TerminalDxe/TerminalConIn.c b/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Console/TerminalDxe/TerminalConIn.c
index 204d599..3aec5e5 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Console/TerminalDxe/TerminalConIn.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Console/TerminalDxe/TerminalConIn.c
@@ -183,6 +183,26 @@ IsKeyRegistered (
   ShiftState      = RegisteredData->KeyState.KeyShiftState | EFI_SHIFT_STATE_VALID;
   InputShiftState = InputData->KeyState.KeyShiftState | EFI_SHIFT_STATE_VALID;
 
+  //
+  // A terminal sends Ctrl+A to Ctrl+Z as the control characters 0x01-0x1A,
+  // and carries no shift state: a key TerminalDxe reads never has one. A key
+  // registered with only Control held (left, right or both), as the UEFI
+  // Shell registers Ctrl-C (0x03) and Ctrl-S (0x13), matches such a
+  // character. Not Backspace, Tab, LF or CR (0x08, 0x09, 0x0A, 0x0D): a
+  // terminal sends those for keys of their own, and plain typing must not
+  // fire a Ctrl+H, Ctrl+I, Ctrl+J or Ctrl+M registration. Any other shift
+  // state must still match exactly, so RCtrl+n does not fire on a plain 'n'
+  // (issue #12281).
+  //
+  if ((InputShiftState == EFI_SHIFT_STATE_VALID) &&
+      (InputData->Key.UnicodeChar >= 0x01) && (InputData->Key.UnicodeChar <= 0x1A) &&
+      (InputData->Key.UnicodeChar != CHAR_BACKSPACE) && (InputData->Key.UnicodeChar != CHAR_TAB) &&
+      (InputData->Key.UnicodeChar != CHAR_LINEFEED) && (InputData->Key.UnicodeChar != CHAR_CARRIAGE_RETURN) &&
+      ((ShiftState & ~(EFI_LEFT_CONTROL_PRESSED | EFI_RIGHT_CONTROL_PRESSED)) == EFI_SHIFT_STATE_VALID))
+  {
+    ShiftState = InputShiftState;
+  }
+
   if ((ShiftState != InputShiftState) ||
       (RegisteredData->KeyState.KeyToggleState != InputData->KeyState.KeyToggleState))
   {
@@ -387,7 +407,9 @@ TerminalConInRegisterKeyNotify (
     // Shift state and toggle state are not transferred via serial lines, so
     // the notification functions for the keys with nonzero KeyShiftState or
     // KeyToggleState will never trigger with this implementation of SimpleTextInEx
-    // protocol.
+    // protocol. The exception: IsKeyRegistered matches a control character
+    // 0x01-0x1A other than BS, TAB, LF and CR, registered with only Control
+    // held and no toggle state, to the character alone.
     //
     DEBUG ((
       DEBUG_VERBOSE,
